<title>INDIA: All Indian exchanges to go on-line by June-SEBI.</title>
<headline>All Indian exchanges to go on-line by June-SEBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's market regulator, the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI), on Wednesday said all the country's 22 stock exchanges would offer screen based trading by June.</p>
<p>Currently only 16 exchanges offer on-line trading facility, the regulatory authority said.</p>
<p>&quot;The remaining stock exchanges ...(are) committed to start on-line screen based trading by end of June, 1997&quot;, SEBI said in a statement after a day-long meeting with officials from the 22 exchanges.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
